**Jonathan Bailey — 31/100 — PASS.** Packet saved to `docs/content-analysis/entity-gaps/Jonathan-Bailey.md`.

He is the anti-Jordi. Everything about him is right except the one thing that has to be right.

**What killed it — the SERP (2/25).** Bailey doesn't just have a personal Wikipedia page. He has *three*: the main article, plus dedicated satellite pages enumerating his awards and his performances. Add IMDb (with its own `/bio/` URL), TMDB, BroadwayWorld, Tribute, Famous Birthdays, a Deadline tag archive, and his verified Instagram. All five SERP audit questions came back unfavorable. A reader needs exactly one click to learn his birth date, hometown, schooling, stage career, screen career, awards, and orientation.

**What was genuinely good:**
- **Source depth 14/15** — GQ, Esquire, and Observer cover interviews all in 2025, the Evening Standard privacy quote, Chicken Shop Date, the People SMOTY package. The gate passes easily.
- **A real contradiction (8/10)** — the man paid to be desired (Anthony, Fiyero, Sexiest Man Alive, the Armani face) who fences off the one relationship that would make the desire concrete, then walks away at peak desirability to staff a nonprofit called *Shameless*. That's an ownable thesis, not a fact collection.

**Timing is also bad (2/10).** The SMOTY spike was November 2025 — nine months stale. 2026 is his self-declared release-free year. The next scheduled catalyst is a 2027 West End run with Ariana Grande.

Two things worth flagging:

**I waived three optional penalties and documented why**, so nobody re-litigates them. The big one: the "-15, attention peaked" penalty doesn't apply, because his name demand *is* durable — durability is the problem here, not the absence of it. He's well-known *and* well-served. Applying it would double-count timing. Even waiving all three, the 2/25 on SERP weakness is decisive alone.

**One unchecked variable:** I did not verify current *Bridgerton* season status. It's the only thing that could move the demand read, so I flagged it in the packet rather than guessing.

If Bailey ever gets overridden into production as a *demand* play rather than a gap play, the packet records the conditions — thesis-first, never a general biography, and a hard prohibition on the James Ellis partner claim, which is tabloid-sourced from a 2019 awards moment and has never been confirmed. The record is openly contradictory there (2023 "lovely man" vs. July 2025 "available"); the correct answer is "not publicly established."

